// The smuggling family — the shared core of Green Lane and its variant lattice
// (`experiments/green-lane/`). "The merchant commits a shipment; the inspector
// waves or opens it" is the sentence a member's `uses smuggling` line stands in
// for, and this file is that sentence written out.
//
// WHY A LIBRARY FOR A NON-CORPUS FAMILY LIVES BESIDE THE CORPUS. Green Lane is
// deliberately an experiment, not a corpus game (`experiments/green-lane/
// DESIGN.md`). `docs/libraries/` is nonetheless where this belongs, because it
// is the only path a `uses` line resolves through (`cardlang/libraries.py`) and
// the tier already wants one loader fewer rather than one more (issue #180). It
// is maintained with the family it serves, and `tests/test_smuggling_library.py`
// binds it against every member so it cannot rot unnoticed.
//
// WHAT IS HERE is the whole smuggling round: the commit — the merchant's
// concealed choice of shipment, forced when one card remains — the inspector's
// response, the wave, and the inspection. Every member holds the first three
// identically. The inspection varies across the family in three orthogonal
// ways: the fine, which contraband the inspector seizes, and what a false
// alarm costs (a fine, and in the bounty variants a token the merchant
// receives). The fine is a per-game constant, so it rides on required state.
// The contraband test is a card predicate, so the game defines it as a
// function. The false-alarm cost is statements, so the game defines it as a
// procedure. The library holds the move that is the same, and its contract
// names the three parts that are the game's.

library smuggling {

  // What the including game must declare or define. The zones are the ones
  // these definitions move cards between; `merchant` and `inspector` are the
  // role pronouns they act for; `tokens` is what an inspection spends;
  // `fine_net` and `fine` are the fines ledger and a seizure's fine; and the
  // last two rows are the game's own rules of inspection.
  //
  // A zone type fixes the per-observer projection, so contracting for
  // `HiddenPile` rather than `PublicHand` is this library saying what its
  // definitions were written against: a waved shipment slides into the
  // warehouse UNSEEN, and a member that declared those piles public would be a
  // different game wearing the same import.
  requires {
    hand[player]      : Hand<player>
    shipment[player]  : HiddenPile<player>
    warehouse[player] : HiddenPile<player>
    cleared[player]   : PlayerPile<player>
    seized[player]    : PlayerPile<player>
    merchant          : Player
    inspector         : Player
    tokens[player]    : Integer
    fine_net[player]  : Integer
    fine              : Integer
    is_contraband(card : Card) : Boolean   // which goods the inspector seizes
    settle_false_alarm() : Procedure       // what an innocent shipment costs
  }

  // The merchant commits one card face down. With one card left the shipment is
  // forced, so no decision is offered and no information is created; otherwise
  // the `as` block makes the merchant the chooser, and the choice is the game's
  // only source of hidden information.
  procedure commit_shipment() {
    if (number of cards in hand[merchant]) is 1 {
      move one card from hand[merchant] to shipment[merchant]
    } else {
      as merchant {
        move chosen 1 card from hand[merchant] to shipment[merchant]
      }
    }
  }

  // The inspector's half of a smuggling round, run after `commit_shipment`.
  // The inspector decides only while they hold a token — with none left the
  // wave is automatic.
  procedure respond() {
    if tokens[inspector] > 0 {
      offer to inspector one of [inspect, wave]
    } else {
      move all cards from shipment[merchant] to warehouse[merchant]
    }
  }

  // Wave the shipment through: it lands in the warehouse still face down — the
  // inspector never learns what it was.
  move_type wave {
    effect {
      move all cards from shipment[merchant] to warehouse[merchant]
    }
  }

  // Spend a token and open the crate. Contraband is seized — it will score for
  // the inspector — and the merchant pays the fine. Legal goods clear publicly,
  // and the false alarm costs whatever the game's `settle_false_alarm` says.
  move_type inspect {
    when: tokens[actor] > 0   // backstop: the offer site in respond() gates on tokens
    effect {
      tokens[actor] -= 1
      reveal one card from shipment[merchant]
      if any card in shipment[merchant] where is_contraband(card) {
        move all cards from shipment[merchant] to seized[actor]
        fine_net[merchant] -= fine
        fine_net[actor] += fine
      } else {
        move all cards from shipment[merchant] to cleared[merchant]
        run settle_false_alarm()
      }
    }
  }
}
